] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487214 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "83eacc45-d857-565f-946e-439539864205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487229 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186486745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487229 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487229 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487229 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186486745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487229 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a1b142ab-d4d9-5382-9f40-a044ab401784" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487274 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487274 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487274 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487274 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186487113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487274 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f39b1857-9db3-543c-8023-433cabfb635c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487292 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487292 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487292 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487292 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487292 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11666770-4f2b-5054-898a-6ed32728d68e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487292 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=2{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 2{x}^{2}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{2})^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{6}}{3}-(\\frac{2{e}^{6}}{9}-\\frac{2}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(12{e}^{6}-2{e}^{6}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(5{e}^{6}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487307 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487307 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487307 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487307 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487307 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2827cc9e-45ac-55e8-ad01-41ef4d905442" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487307 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,(x){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}x(\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(({e}^{3})^{2})\\,({e}^{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})\\,(1)]-2{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{6})-2x{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =6{e}^{3}-2({e}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487315 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487315 #edb/ref 1069 "q-30481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487315 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487315 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487315 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "328d9940-84c5-5488-9fa8-98ff5e7ef880" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487315 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x+1} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\,{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\cdot x-\\int x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\int \\frac{x}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use a substitution $x+1=u,$ thus $x=u-1$ and $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\int \\frac{x}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\int \\frac{u-1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-\\int \\,\\text{d}u+\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{u} \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-u+\\operatorname{ln}⁡u+D \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+D \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)-x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=D-1$ is an integral constant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487317 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487317 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487317 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487317 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487317 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c9f18f7-85c5-5539-81bc-9088568cf461" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487317 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}={x}^{-2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{-2}\\,dx=-{x}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(-{x}^{-1}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}(-{x}^{-1})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{{e}^{2}}-(-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{1})]+{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})}{{e}^{2}}+(-{x}^{-1}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{e}^{2}}+(-\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+1) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487352 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350963" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487352 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}6\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99bfd564-d6cc-54a4-9108-196e20d54d83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487352 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=6\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 6\\sqrt{x}\\,dx=4{x}^{3/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}6\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})(4{x}^{3/2}){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}(4{x}^{3/2})(\\frac{2}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[4{e}^{3/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-4(1)^{3/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1)^{2})]-8{\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{e}^{3/2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-\\frac{16{x}^{3/2}}{3}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{4}} \\\\  & =8{e}^{3/2}-(\\frac{16{e}^{3/2}}{3}-\\frac{16}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(24{e}^{3/2}-16{e}^{3/2}+16) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8{e}^{3/2}+16) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}({e}^{3/2}+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487357 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487357 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487357 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487357 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int 4{x}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487357 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9e36e24a-9d09-5b52-9d60-57f7f164fe98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487357 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{4}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{7}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{8}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{x}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})(\\frac{{x}^{8}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{8}}{2})(\\frac{4}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})}{2}-2\\int {x}^{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{4})}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{8}}{4}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487389 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487389 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351045" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487389 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487389 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487389 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dec6c4d2-4bd8-5abe-a87c-7b60b0c36fa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487389 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int 1\\cdot \\,dx=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{3})\\,(x){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}x(\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[{log}_{5}⁡(({e}^{3})^{3})\\,({e}^{3})-{log}_{5}⁡({1}^{3})\\,(1)]-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{3}{log}_{5}⁡({e}^{9})-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}x{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}({e}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{6{e}^{3}+3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487393 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186487214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487393 #edb/ref 1069 "q-12571" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487393 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487393 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(5x)}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487393 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2daa4c1-fd00-5b69-bf1e-328646061d80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186487393 #edb/ref 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡(5x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=2\\sqrt{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(5x)}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡(5x))(2\\sqrt{x})-\\int (2\\sqrt{x})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{x}{log}_{2}⁡(5x)-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-\\frac{4\\sqrt{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)-2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
